[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Frontend Performance Testing: Core Web Vitals, Lighthouse, and RUM"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Frontend performance directly impacts user experience, conversion rates, and search engine rankings. Modern web performance testing goes beyond simple load times, focusing on user-centric metrics known as Core Web Vitals, automated lab testing via Lighthouse, and real-world user monitoring (RUM)."},{"order":3,"type":"heading","text":"Understanding Core Web Vitals"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Core Web Vitals are a set of standardized metrics established by Google that quantify the key user experience dimensions on the web:"},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Largest Contentful Paint (LCP): Measures perceived load speed. It marks the point in the page load timeline when the main content has likely loaded. Good: <= 2.5 seconds."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Interaction to Next Paint (INP): Assesses page responsiveness by observing the latency of all click, tap, and keyboard interactions throughout the user's lifecycle. Good: <= 200 milliseconds."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS): Measures visual stability by quantifying unexpected layout shifts of visible elements. Good: <= 0.1."},{"order":8,"type":"heading","text":"Lab Testing with Lighthouse"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"Lighthouse is an automated, open-source tool for improving the quality of web pages. It runs audits for performance, accessibility, progressive web apps, SEO, and more in a controlled, simulated environment (Lab Data)."},{"order":10,"type":"subheading","text":"Running Lighthouse via CLI"},{"order":11,"type":"paragraph","text":"You can integrate Lighthouse into your CI/CD pipelines using the Node CLI package to catch performance regressions early."},{"order":12,"type":"code","text":"npm install -g lighthouse
lighthouse https://example.com --view --preset=desktop"},{"order":13,"type":"heading","text":"Real User Monitoring (RUM)"},{"order":14,"type":"paragraph","text":"While Lighthouse provides consistent lab metrics, it cannot replicate the infinite variety of real-world devices, network conditions, and user behaviors. RUM collects telemetry data from actual users visiting your production application."},{"order":15,"type":"subheading","text":"Measuring Core Web Vitals in JavaScript"},{"order":16,"type":"paragraph","text":"You can use the official web-vitals library to capture real user metrics and send them to your analytics endpoint."},{"order":17,"type":"code","text":"import {onLCP, onINP, onCLS} from 'web-vitals';

function sendToAnalytics(metric) {
  const body = JSON.stringify(metric);
  // Use navigator.sendBeacon() to reliably send data on page unload
  navigator.sendBeacon('/analytics', body);
}

onLCP(sendToAnalytics);
onINP(sendToAnalytics);
onCLS(sendToAnalytics);"},{"order":18,"type":"heading","text":"Best Practices for Frontend Performance"},{"order":19,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Optimize and properly size images using modern formats like WebP or AVIF."},{"order":20,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Implement code-splitting and lazy-load non-critical JavaScript and images."},{"order":21,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Minimize main-thread work by breaking up long tasks and deferring non-essential scripts."},{"order":22,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Preload critical assets like fonts, hero images, and stylesheets using <link rel="preload">."}]
